          "path": "_m/g/f/j/c/broughty-castle-wp/broughty-castle-geograph-org-u.jpg",
          "filename": "Broughty Castle - geograph.org.uk - 7506.jpg",
          "caption": "Broughty Castle. Broughty Castle sits imposingly at the mouth of the Tay. Built in 1496 on a rocky promontory, it has faced many sieges and battles. These have left their scars - marks made by cannon shot are still visible. During the eighteenth century it fell into ruin, to be rebuilt in the 1860s as part of the Crimean War effort. Broughty Castle Museum houses fascinating displays on the life and times of Broughty Ferry, its people, the environment and the wildlife that live close by.",
          "alt": "Broughty Castle. Broughty Castle sits imposingly at the mouth of the Tay. Built in 1496 on a rocky promontory, it has faced many sieges and battles. These have left their scars - marks made by cannon shot are still visible. During the eighteenth century it fell into ruin, to be rebuilt in the 1860s as part of the Crimean War effort. Broughty Castle Museum houses fascinating displays on the life and times of Broughty Ferry, its people, the environment and the wildlife that live close by.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 480,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
