          "filename": "Broughty Castle - geograph.org.uk - 1061603.jpg",
          "caption": "Broughty Castle A 15th century construction after changing hands over the years. It was acquired in 1855 by the War Office to protect the harbour from the Russians. soon the threat was from the French and much extra defences were constructed. Submarine miners were based here from the 1880s to lay mines in the Tay to destroy enemy shipping. It opened as a museum in 1969.",
